==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mey- (change)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|submitten}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|submittere}}, infinitive of {{m|la|submittō||place under, yield}}, from {{m|la|sub||under, from below, up}} + {{m|la|mitto||to send}}. Compare {{m|en|upsend}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|səbmĭtʹ}}, {{IPA|en|/səbˈmɪt/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪt|s=2}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-submit.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|sub|mit}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|++}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[yield]] or [[give way]] to another.
#: {{ux|en|They will not '''submit''' to the destruction of their rights.}}
#: {{ux|en|We '''submit''' to their superior judgment.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To yield (something) to another, as when defeated.
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To enter or put forward for approval, consideration, marking etc.
#: {{ux|en|I '''submit''' these plans for your approval.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1843|author=w:Thomas Macaulay|title=Sir James Mackintosh's History of the Revolution
|passage=We '''submit''' that a wooden spoon of our day would not be justified in calling Galileo and Napier blockheads because they never heard of the differential calculus.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 September 23|author=Paul Bigland|title=The tragic tale of the Tay Bridge disaster|journal=RAIL|page=82|text=Determined to learn from Bouch's mistakes, they conducted a through {{sic}} survey of the riverbed. Having learned what they needed to know, they '''submitted''' plans for a new double-track bridge by the end of 1880.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Ashley Killough and Ed Lavandera|title=Another education fight over DEI emerges, this time at a conservative campus in Texas|url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/02/15/us/texas-education-fight-diversity-equity-inclusion/index.html|date=2023-02-15|passage=The biology department at Texas Tech University – set in deeply conservative West Texas – asked faculty candidates in 2021 to '''submit''' statements on their commitment to DEI.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231117042622/https://www.cnn.com/2023/02/15/us/texas-education-fight-diversity-equity-inclusion/index.html|archivedate=17 November 2023}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Katherine Dillinger|title=House Covid-19 panel releases final report criticizing public health response to the pandemic|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/12/02/health/house-covid-subcommittee-report/index.html|date=2024-12-02|passage=The subcommittee, which is chaired by Ohio Republican Rep. Brad Wenstrup, a podiatrist, will hold a markup session for the report Wednesday before '''submitting''' it to the congressional record.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260611105339/https://www.cnn.com/2024/12/02/health/house-covid-subcommittee-report/index.html|archivedate=11 June 2026}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[subject]]; to put through a process.
#: {{ux|en|I was '''submit'''ted to a binding pledge.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1859|author=Victor Regnault|title=Elements of Chemistry|passage=[Skins] must be '''submitted''' to several washings, treadings, and stretchings, before they acquire the necessary pliancy.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|mixed martial arts|professional wrestling}} To win a fight against (an opponent) by [[submission]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To let down; to lower.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1662|author=w:John Dryden|title=Poem to the Lord Chancellor Hyde
|passage=Sometimes the hill '''submits''' itself a while.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To put or place under.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1611|author=w:George Chapman|title=Homer's Iliads
|passage=The bristled throat / Of the '''submitted''' sacrifice with ruthless steel he cut.}}

